  "details": "Edit: So it turns out I was wrong. It is just applying the SteamVR finger tracking data by default. You can disable this by disabling \"Avatars Use Finger Tracking\" under the \"Controls\" tab in the Settings.\n\nHowever, I hope to leave this feedback here in case other people come across this issue.\n\nHere's the FAQ: https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/input-20-faq\n\n---\n\nIt appears that the default hand gestures for Quest are broken. \n\nWith the hand in the neutral rest position, the index finger is curled and the thumb is pushed out.\n\nWith the grip activated, the fingers dig into the palm.\n\nIt was not like this before the update.",
